**DI registration** (add to `Program.cs` or `Startup.cs`):

```csharp
builder.Services.AddSingleton<IEnvironmentProvider, EnvironmentProvider>();
```

**Usage in your class:**

```csharp
public class MyService(IEnvironmentProvider environment)
{
    public void DoWork()
    {
        var value = environment.GetEnvironmentVariable("MY_VAR");
        var host = environment.MachineName;
    }
}
```

**In tests**, mock `IEnvironmentProvider` with your preferred mocking library (e.g. Moq/NSubstitute) or a simple hand-rolled fake. The wrapper is stateless so `AddSingleton` is correct.
